# ALLOWLIST by default: `COPY . /app` builds a PUBLIC image, so exclude EVERYTHING
# and re-include only what the build needs. A denylist ships any new local file the
# operator forgets to list (a stray .env, a scratch script, a review harness); an
# allowlist ships nothing unless it is named here. Verify after a build with
#   podman run --rm <img> ls -la /app
# that only the entries below are present.
*

# What the image actually needs:
#   pyproject.toml            - pip install -e . (also reads README.md + LICENSE)
#   src/                      - the assay package (incl. lm_eval_tasks/*.yaml package data)
#   scripts/pod_entry.sh      - chmod'd + ENTRYPOINT
!pyproject.toml
!README.md
!LICENSE
!src/
!scripts/

# Re-exclude junk that lives INSIDE the re-included dirs (later rules win).
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/*.safetensors
